Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Nothing below is vendored into this repository. The managed build resolves its
dependencies through NuGet. The console ports fetch theirs at build time, check
them against a pinned SHA-256 and compile them from source into a gitignored
directory. This is an inventory, not a licence grant: each component is governed
by its own licence and carries its own notices. The reasoning behind the
decisions recorded here is in ports/ripcord-ps3/README.md ("Licensing") and in
the comments of ports/ripcord-ps3/tools/gen-third-party-notices.sh.

Managed build (Windows)

  NuGet packages resolved at build time, and Microsoft platform components: the
  Windows App SDK, Media Foundation, Direct3D 12, WASAPI and GameInput. Their
  licences are reproduced in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt, which ships beside the app
  and is generated from the packages that ship by tools/third-party-notices.

Console ports, fetched and built from source

  openh264 2.6.0    BSD-2-Clause   ports/ripcord-ps3/tools/build-openh264.sh
  Opus 1.5.2        BSD-3-Clause   ports/ripcord-ps3/tools/build-opus.sh
  Mbed TLS 2.28.8   Apache-2.0     libripcord/tools/build-mbedtls.sh
                    (elected - see below)

  Each script pins a version and a digest and refuses a mismatch. ripcord-ps3
  builds all three; ripcord-3ds links devkitPro's builds of Opus and the same
  Mbed TLS version; the host test suite builds Mbed TLS for the machine running
  it. ports/ripcord-ps3/DECODE.md records why a permissive-only line was held
  for these and why an LGPL decoder was declined.

Brand artwork, fetched when the wordmark is redrawn

  Outfit 1.100      OFL-1.1        brand/outline-wordmark.py
  Copyright 2021 The Outfit Project Authors
  (https://github.com/Outfitio/Outfit-Fonts)

  The wordmark in brand/ripcord-wordmark.svg and the two brand/ripcord-lockup
  SVGs is Outfit SemiBold converted to plain outlines. The font itself is not
  in this repository and does not ship with the app: the script fetches it,
  with its OFL.txt, from a pinned google/fonts commit into the gitignored
  brand/third-party/, and refuses a SHA-256 mismatch. The licence places no
  condition on artwork made with the font, and the font declares no Reserved
  Font Name.

Console toolchain libraries, statically linked

  ripcord-ps3 links PSL1GHT (MIT), FreeType and zlib from the ps3dev toolchain;
  ripcord-3ds links devkitPro's libctru and its builds of Opus and Mbed TLS.
  They come from the installed toolchain rather than this repository, so no
  version or digest is pinned here. Beyond those named, the toolchain
  components' licences have not been separately catalogued; that belongs with
  a binary release.

Licence elections, recorded so they are choices rather than defaults

  Mbed TLS is offered under Apache-2.0 or GPL-2.0-or-later. RIPCORD ELECTS
  APACHE-2.0. FreeType is offered under the FreeType License or GPLv2. RIPCORD
  ELECTS THE FREETYPE LICENSE. In each case the GPL arm is not compatible with
  the Apache-2.0 licence this project is distributed under. Upstream's Mbed TLS
  licence file carries both arms, so the GPL text travels inside every
  ripcord-ps3 package as upstream's own unmodified text, and the generated
  notices say so at the head of that section. openh264 and Opus are
  single-licence. FTL section 3 forbids using the FreeType Team's name for
  promotion without permission; nothing in this project does.

Notices that ship in every ripcord-ps3 package

  USRDIR/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt is generated at package time by
  ports/ripcord-ps3/tools/gen-third-party-notices.sh from the licence texts of
  the exact versions linked; the generator fails the build if a licence that
  requires reproduction (openh264, Opus, Mbed TLS) is missing. Two texts are
  emitted by the generator itself rather than read from the toolchain, which
  ships no licence files: PSL1GHT's MIT notice, headed with the revision built
  from, and FreeType's required credit and disclaimer:

      Portions of this software are copyright (c) 2026 The FreeType Project
      (https://freetype.org). All rights reserved.

      This software is based in part on the work of the FreeType Team.

  The .pkg is what this project publishes, as CI artifacts and as release
  assets, and it carries these notices inside it, so the obligations above are
  this project's own. The bare .self is not published: it links the same
  components and carries no notice text, so it stays a local build product.
  ripcord-3ds has no equivalent yet, and no .3dsx is released. (The dotnet
  client's THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt is committed so it can ship in the release
  zip; it is generated the same way and regenerated when the packages change.)

Console firmware, used at runtime and never redistributed

  The ports reach their console's own system modules through the toolchain's
  stub libraries. ripcord-ps3 also reads the system typeface from /dev_flash at
  runtime and rasterises it with FreeType; the typeface stays on the console.
  No firmware component - no module, no font, no data file - is copied into
  this repository or into a built binary.
